Fillets: a rounding whose edge ends where a convex crease of its face
begins: the ball turned on about the crease into the face at the end
(mitcad#1434).

A tube's outside (a cylinder Fs) meets a plane Fk along a line L at a
convex crease of 30 degrees; L runs square to the tube's end plane Fop and
ends on it at the vertex V where Fop's rim (its edge with Fs) ends. The
rim is rounded with R. The rounding's contact on Fs reaches L at the
section through V, at P, R from V; its contact on Fop lies inside Fop.
OCCT ran the rim's torus on past V (the spine prolonged) and cut it by Fk
(its plane cuts the torus from P to Fop's edge with Fk): the end stood out
of the body past Fk and the result was invalid. The stored body after the
rounding ends the torus at V's section and closes the corner with a horn
torus about L at P (major and minor radius R): the ball rolled on over L,
touching Fop, until its centre lies in Fk's plane, where Fk's corner at V
is cut along the ball's circle. Fk is a strip there: the other tube lies
beyond Fk's plane, and the cut of the torus by Fk would leave Fk. Where
the cut stays on Fk (the same design's other tube, its rims ending at a
crease of 70.5 degrees), the stored body has the torus cut by Fk, as OCCT
makes it.

- PerformPivotAboutCreaseAtEnd (1220's ball turning about a crease at the
  end) also takes the vertex at L's own end (before: left to the faces
  beyond L): Fk a plane through L, the face at the end, any convex crease
  between Fs and Fk short of a right angle (at a right angle the section
  is Fk's plane), P R from the vertex on L, where the end piece runs on
  past the section and Fk's cut of it leaves Fk (ChFi3d_CutLeavesFace:
  points of the cut between its ends, found from the chord by projecting
  on the blend's surface and on Fk's plane in turn, outside Fk); elsewhere
  Fk cuts the end as before. The ball turns from the
  section towards Fk's side of L (tk, the direction in Fk square to L at
  less than a right angle to the ball's centre from P) by pi / 2 less the
  crease. Fk's cut is the torus's tube circle in Fk's plane (a section of
  the torus by a plane through its axis, at its apex, is not found by
  BRepAlgoAPI_Section), from P to Fop, built as a circle over the
  parameters 3 pi / 4 to 5 pi / 4 with its curve on the torus a line in
  one B-spline span over them, so that both reverse alike.
- That end piece (an analytic blend run on past the section through the
  vertex and cut by Fk there, its contact on Fop ending on Fop's edge with
  Fk) is cut back to the section: the other contact's point on the section
  taken from its curve, its interference's parameter and the piece's spine
  parameter set there when the end is built.

